Description: UPS, OLED and fan daemon and tools for Argon40 Raspberry Pi cases
 argon-utils replaces the vendor's Python stack for Argon40 enclosures and
 the Argon PWR UPS with a Rust implementation: a daemon (argond), a command
 line tool (argonctl), a desktop notification agent and a panel icon
 (argon-tray).
 .
 The daemon monitors the UPS over its USB serial link and, when the battery is
 confirmed critical, schedules a delayed poweroff that restoring mains cancels.
 It also drives the case fan on models that have an Argon MCU, and reports the
 kernel-controlled fan on models that do not, such as the ONE V5 with a Pi 5.
 .
 Nothing that changes device state happens until the operator sets a mode other
 than read-only in /etc/argon-utils/config.toml.
